		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=34045#p34045"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>super il est passé leader <img src="http://forums.postgresql.fr/img/smilies/big_smile.png" width="15" height="15" alt="big_smile" /><br />bon par contre j arrive pas a connecté le 2ème dessus maintenant ....</p><p>root@div2sv002597:/bases/pgsql/14/data# patronictl -c /etc/patroni/patroni.yml list<br />+ Cluster: clusterig9 (7191794644507281311) ---+---------+----+-----------+<br />| Member&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;| Host&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; | Role&#160; &#160; | State&#160; &#160;| TL | Lag in MB |<br />+--------------+---------------------+---------+---------+----+-----------+<br />| ig9-cluster1 | 172.18.239.151:5434 | Leader&#160; | running |&#160; 2 |&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;|<br />| ig9-cluster2 | 172.18.239.153:5434 | Replica | stopped |&#160; &#160; |&#160; &#160;unknown |<br />+--------------+---------------------+---------+---------+----+-----------+<br />root@div2sv002597:/bases/pgsql/14/data# ll<br />total 0</p><p>sur le secondaire , j&#039;ai lancer la commande suivante: <br /> patronictl -c /etc/patroni/patroni.yml reinit clusterig9 ig9-cluster2</p><p>et dans la log patroni.log j&#039;ai le message suivant:</p><p>OSError: [Errno 16] Device or resource busy: &#039;/bases/pgsql/14/data/&#039;</p><p>/bases/pgsql/14/data/ est un fs ... cela peu venir de la ????</p><p>merci de votre aide<br />Katia</p>]]></content>
